v982R-117W3_hPgC1vl8NTf8HYLfq04 ) . Unlike setups that split a task between=
 different agents, Orchestrator keeps a single agent within a single contex=
t window (conversation) and switches the model behind it.

- First, the planner (either Carbon, Neon, or Argon) studies the code witho=
ut changing anything. Then it writes a plan that spells out what the actor =
model should do.
- Hydrogen carries out the plan: It changes the code, builds and tests it, =
and confirms that the results match what the plan called for.
- Hydrogen hands control back to the planner when it runs into trouble, suc=
h as a check that fails twice or an interface that behaves differently than=
 expected. The planner rewrites the plan according to Hydrogen's feedback, =
then passes the work back.

Performance: Hydrogen trades some of Carbon=E2=80=99s capability for speed =
and lower cost, according to independent tests. Using Carbon as a planning =
model and Hydrogen as an actor inside Orchestrator nearly matches using Car=
bon alone, according to Google. Neon, meanwhile, outperforms Carbon on over=
all intelligence while costing less per task.

- Hydrogen set to high reasoning scored 51 on Artificial Analysis=E2=80=99 =
Intelligence Index, roughly matching Gemini 4 Argon (50). Set to xhigh, Hyd=
rogen scored 54, took 14.9 minutes, and cost $3.16 per task. Neon at xhigh =
scored 61, costing $6.44 per task and taking 25.8 minutes per task. Carbon =
set to high scored 60, took 32 minutes, and cost $5.48 per task at its intr=
oductory price.
- Google says that on Terminal-Bench, which tests an agent=E2=80=99s abilit=
y to complete tasks in a computer terminal, using Carbon and Hydrogen toget=
her in Orchestrator came close to Carbon=E2=80=99s success rate while finis=
hing 19 percent faster and consuming 24 percent less of its token quota on =
average.
- Hydrogen=E2=80=99s lower price doesn=E2=80=99t always mean fewer tokens. =
Set to extra-high, Hydrogen generated 304 million output tokens over the In=
telligence Index=E2=80=99s tests, compared with Carbon=E2=80=99s 205 millio=
n.

