-hs-cos-general-type=3D"widget" data-hs-cos-type=3D"rich_text"><h1 style=3D=
"margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height:125%; font=
-size:32px; font-weight:bold">Carbon, Hydrogen, Neon, Oh My!</h1>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Google introduced two faster, less expensive =
Gemini 4 models and a way for its coding agent to hand work back and forth =
between models mid-task.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><strong>What's new:</strong> On November 12, =
Google released <a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC=
404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF4g5nR3bW50kH_H6lZ3kZW7ntWcf3=
lv8SGW8FPpqM150N9hN45zsDkSkn3HW7bDRP33Py1jDW37ByNG5Qd9wpV6TSsG6hbmmRW4fQxCV=
15WPgZW55xQTv2GDSP0W2wPGFL2zl317W3cVJLT4VZmvbW5QlMLk4PfPgPW5_8P0y5Lb9htW3fs=
7tn2DBVkYW4fB2XV1B1bRwW8jjVgg4w5T0PN4jHGzDBpBrjV4nlp32Zxk-YW63--1R7Gb1L3W44=
qg-k4XCDR2N48jhH7zpL7sN7k9c65LDjgYW6-2pg66HVFrsW7Jfr0-3tndj6VVR4g-2dnlGMN1s=
rr8DZTWyYW6T_nKp5452mWW6gHSCS8zxWPJW8VcLjN2hBw2lW612mKb8P1Fn_W1mcqL911BGxhN=
1tw53SvC1MwW8TqGfv4w9dmNf3mRmgW04" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=
=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"4ImJJNRl" target=3D"_blank">Gemini 4 Hydrogen<=
/a>, a model built to carry out coding and other agentic tasks quickly and =
at lower cost than Gemini 4 Carbon. On November 18, the company added <a hr=
ef=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz=
8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF4g5nR3bW50kH_H6lZ3pKW89mQTy6Z-z4XW88GdQW1J0Hr6V8x=
kqm4DGDkGW68hrmy2VLkzWMndsJ9X4NMDW1mmfyf85vMk5W6CCzq97l4jfnW5LQJlL5jJVxHVpl=
9N41KD-m_W72T2_W5cjQL0W2pprgC8801LPW2gxdGG6BBWlFW5gFPwt3yh9K8W1LN4fJ1621FQV=
3Bw305PytGzW3g7htB59jWqCW71g4rx2bCgt4W1hfpz-32KqzXN7ljKWRkYDymN2536-Xp-drnV=
Sj5Fg8r9VtdW4v8wWW4TWk5sW3HGyR23XM8VkW43DhZG3fDr3WVXw0fq8MWHl0W7ypZbs4H8R6s=
N3-mB3v4GTjXW4wFgps19B-srW7BcdK02dkZyHW6qjbfF4F6Q8YVwFvQy1-r0qZW1PKsg81QDFp=
_f5FPP7T04" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v=
2=3D"7Es3Cz6y" target=3D"_blank">Gemini 4 Neon</a>, a model that rivals Car=
bon=E2=80=99s performance at an intermediate speed and cost. In addition, A=
ntigravity, Google=E2=80=99s counterpart to OpenAI's Codex and Anthropic=E2=
=80=99s Claude Code, gained Orchestrator, an option that allows larger mode=
ls like Carbon or Neon to plan a task and have smaller models like Hydrogen=
 carry it out.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li><strong>Input/output:</strong> Text, images, audio, and video in, text =
out (up to 1 million tokens of input and output combined; up to 64,000 outp=
ut token by default</li>
<li><strong>Speed: </strong>Hydrogen,<strong><span style=3D"white-space-col=
lapse: preserve;"> </span></strong>173 tokens per second at its highest set=
ting; Neon, 99 tokens per second, both according to Artificial Analysis</li=
>
<li><strong>Architecture:</strong><span style=3D"white-space-collapse: pres=
erve;"> </span><a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC4=
04/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF4g5nR3bW50kH_H6lZ3pVW7w79hb5s=
wWwTW4zyVkZ3Z-bYgN6ZFzdppwhNSW1w8LTJ41TH0BW3KdgWx7d_F67W3xbwr96ZwrJtW1nvXXg=
7Ndh2vW37M_JM2VX39VW87zm1k4njzXXW2xrKRr95N98rW4kZ3--3VLrpgW5XQn5t5tPc4pN2dr=
HsMZXmsXW88lJ0F2qxqdZW4NkG-B8GlR4TW3w-rNy7WC5YJW5kQGj574cxCYW3S4-Ht1RZQhDW5=
Y6z_N7NcLDgVX96Yk94KTQjVrDxnz73NzpwVLSwRP998kvNW7f3wbt9fFkfYW2lBjBT4mz4-_W3=
zxBzW8XkZ0PW6xVBGd8pbrsJW76vJqd1KYXldW8nDfxG28pbrBW2qjRjW7tBSKcW9gR1wL1rbN0=
hW371_0W4CszqhN8DlN11FgwSRf7s04ns04" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-i=
d=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"U0+XY/0/" target=3D"_blank">Adapted</a> from =
Gemini 4 Carbon</li>
<li><strong>Price: </strong>Hydrogen $1.50/$7.50 per million input/output t=
okens via API; Neon $3.00/$15.00 per million input/tokens</li>
<li><strong>Weights/license:</strong> Proprietary</li>
<li><strong>Undisclosed:</strong> Parameter count, architecture details, ho=
w Google adapted Hydrogen or Neon from Carbon, training data and methods</l=
i>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><strong>How it works:</strong> Orchestrator d=
ivides each task between a planner and an executor instead of running one m=
odel for everything, according to Antigravity=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://=
info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHk=
G5XSKyyN8rPF5M3qgz0W7Y8-PT6lZ3mhN3XSw13p0cnqW7Dd20t7Sh-6qN37zcWmQhWMBW3XxfC=
Z53vH8bW5R54Wy28t5SWW4-g1Yp6KBTrRW5yQz8y4fc94hW3BbtsC1FvkVLW2gyf3G8Yb6dYW2T=
Z25D4LNHpwW7T7nyZ5wk7CVW8YQ8dc1Bv3HvW7lc5cq4ZYDTdN6nRB4V_PJmRN5kq24wCQGLwW4=
_gXlq8C4wPVW5yj5pj8D7BwjW5SF0V18_LTtFW61Nj251QPDGmW2LWWqW1jhRNQW1CjV_f2DHJZ=
MW8LHc831csFkBW8kNwNf6W28H3W7l_mPy7MmjpCW8crdVz7dFBfpW3V-JtL6NTfQ_f799r4H04=
" rel=3D"noopener" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-li=
nk-id-v2=3D"+PZSsxa1" target=3D"_blank">documentation</a>. Unlike setups th=
at split a task between different agents, Orchestrator keeps a single agent=
 within a single context window (conversation) and switches the model behin=
d it.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li>First, the planner (either Carbon, Neon, or Argon) studies the code wit=
hout changing anything. Then it writes a plan that spells out what the acto=
r model should do.</li>
<li>Hydrogen&nbsp;carries out the plan: It changes the code, builds and tes=
ts it, and confirms that the results match what the plan called for.</li>
<li>Hydrogen hands control back to the planner when it runs into trouble, s=
uch as a check that fails twice or an interface that behaves differently th=
an expected. The planner rewrites the plan according to Hydrogen's feedback=
, then passes the work back.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><strong>Performance:</strong> Hydrogen trades=
 some of Carbon=E2=80=99s capability for speed and lower cost, according to=
 independent tests. Using Carbon as a planning model and Hydrogen as an act=
or inside Orchestrator nearly matches using Carbon alone, according to Goog=
le. Neon, meanwhile, outperforms Carbon on overall intelligence while costi=
ng less per task.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li>Hydrogen set to high reasoning scored 51 on Artificial Analysis=E2=80=
=99 Intelligence Index, roughly matching Gemini 4 Argon (50). Set to xhigh,=
 Hydrogen scored 54, took 14.9 minutes, and cost $3.16 per task. Neon at xh=
igh scored 61, costing $6.44 per task and taking 25.8 minutes per task. Car=
bon set to high scored 60,&nbsp;took 32 minutes, and cost $5.48 per task at=
 its introductory price.</li>
<li>Google says that on Terminal-Bench, which tests an agent=E2=80=99s abil=
ity to complete tasks in a computer terminal, using Carbon and Hydrogen tog=
ether in Orchestrator came close to Carbon=E2=80=99s success rate while fin=
ishing 19 percent faster and consuming 24 percent less of its token quota o=
n average.</li>
<li>Hydrogen=E2=80=99s lower price doesn=E2=80=99t always mean fewer tokens=
. Set to extra-high, Hydrogen generated 304 million output tokens over the =
Intelligence Index=E2=80=99s tests, compared with Carbon=E2=80=99s 205 mill=
ion.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><strong>Behind the news:</strong> Google made=
 Gemini 4 <a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX=
9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF623qgz0W8wLKSR6lZ3nCW2N8mrz5ys_-FV=
NZF-97_RzkLVNZbQ53hRsG1W7WVQZF1D59ySW6x_TyL2H6jxCW9gDkm85XL5zWW3FwMm93DFGk1=
W36d_gL6Hv_GKVpFdMs4pZP2jW6m1gKd17dNnBW2YnTDV5kZHcRM3BNdPsszYnW53q89V6LB85w=
W3dsg5_8XP0N_W46H4Gh86tYW6W6HXB022mrtDLW6YQqfT2-y41GW5nbgVs1RvRtBW6tTCNs8qB=
xLMW4vdGQp3J6lDfW4R-8YB7bKwKBW8y_HXR4Q5NkHW5PjtmM7WR0rJW94FCNz1j26JfW95W1XV=
8txyDsW3ZxlfT8vv34tVMf1bM2D8CldW5JNlJ11VzhXKf3Y2WTx04" style=3D"color:#237b=
94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"EKV7YLnU" target=3D"_blank"=
>Carbon</a> widely available on November 10, following Argon in September. =
The power and cost of Gemini=E2=80=99s models roughly correspond with the w=
eight of their element names: Hydrogen is light and fast, while&nbsp;Carbon=
 is relatively heavier and more substantial. But the elementally heavier Ne=
on is faster than Carbon, and Argon, now the least capable of Gemini=E2=80=
=99s =E2=80=9Celement=E2=80=9D models, is heaviest of all.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Pairing a ch=
eaper model with a costlier one isn=E2=80=99t new. Anthropic=E2=80=99s Clau=
de Code offers a related =E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e=
3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF5s3qgz0W7l=
CdLW6lZ3k_VqlNwH7snYKzW1MhhCG7r10wpF2JGW9T2JhSW4c9XCx34_CCnW1nhYzX4bTKlhW4s=
nHrV1dgw_vN8mlzHQbXXCRVJ67-v4l30vFV_ksD979CQgwW96H8s67ytGXrW5T4CRj5SLNN2W6N=
5dd35TWCXTW6V_JLq9dW274W6Zg66j3LgYB_W6KPdZR15pSCmW2xqjk-6f9VCbW1XKN748YwGLz=
VpkBPG293GCVN6--v8ssLnqxW5R-k9-3WkR6BW14vn624V9g7zW4Z-PN68gQPM1W6DQk9Q3Knfl=
BW3pH6ZB7mpNYYf8LQ0Sb04" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data=
-hs-link-id-v2=3D"v9G4oKPB" target=3D"_blank">advisor</a>=E2=80=9D option, =
in which a cheaper model does the work and consults a stronger one at key m=
oments, such as before committing to a plan or when it gets stuck. OpenAI=
=E2=80=99s Codex lets developers assign different models to <a href=3D"http=
s://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8=
