 class=3D"hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_rich_tex=
t" style=3D"color: inherit; font-size: inherit; line-height: inherit;" data=
-hs-cos-general-type=3D"widget" data-hs-cos-type=3D"rich_text"><h1 style=3D=
"margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height:125%; font=
-size:32px; font-weight:bold">How the =E2=80=9CToken Tax=E2=80=9D Hurts Non=
-English Users</h1>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
>&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
>Using AI models costs non-Western speakers in emerging markets far more th=
an they do for English speakers. A recent study quantifies the difference a=
cross more than 200 languages.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
>&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
><strong>What=E2=80=99s new:</strong> All language models break words into =
tokens. But not every language is tokenized equally well. Low-resource lang=
uages are not well-served by popular existing tokenizers. According to a <a=
 href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8=
qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF5M3qgz0W7Y8-PT6lZ3lkW2srfHD7YZr1XW7XHSj42t9Jj8=
W7n8_ll5rKGFmW40B0B538BYTMW1N4Bq32jslyXW3C_Pbf99WcNXW7qN0xv86ryB7VN4_0r7SnN=
d2N7FhBnmPdZQcW64mWTn2Xb4nqW44zRjK2VCVLWW9llJbz8ryGsDW4vQ-3n8V0jMXVbX5QY7fy=
PPXN7k8kgfk3w0HW946l2P39PWNcW4lffNc3CpwKqW28WV7q2JNvvlW1WWz5W6QnZBRW8y-xMG6=
FfPqCW3Pxz3s5TgR3VW3QPbGN7Mq02LW4-wy0n3CZ59jV3HptM3Wt1_SW1ph9685PT14SW3PwHh=
F3k6WWFf5qbTJb04" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-lin=
k-id-v2=3D"4KOvbzoa" target=3D"_blank">study</a> published by the Coalition=
 for Language Equity in AI Research (CLEAR), token counts (and therefore co=
st) for identical content can be up to 17 times higher for the worst-served=
 languages than for the most efficiently tokenized ones.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
>&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
><strong>How it works:</strong> Tokenizers turn text into tokens based on h=
ow frequently sequences of characters appear in an LLM=E2=80=99s training d=
ata. That means that the more often a language=E2=80=99s words appear in a =
data set, the more efficiently that language can be turned into meaningful =
blocks. Meanwhile, languages with less representation are split into much s=
maller segments, leading to significantly higher token counts per word or p=
hrase. This leads to a correspondingly higher cost for the exact same conte=
nt.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li>CLEAR showed that in GPT-5, the same sentence in English (=E2=80=9CPeop=
le should benefit from AI, regardless of the language they speak=E2=80=9D),=
 Malayalam (=E2=80=9C=E0=B4=86=E0=B4=B3=E0=B5=81=E0=B4=95=E0=B5=BE =E0=B4=
=8F=E0=B4=A4=E0=B5=8D =E0=B4=AD=E0=B4=BE=E0=B4=B7 =E0=B4=B8=E0=B4=82=E0=B4=
=B8=E0=B4=BE=E0=B4=B0=E0=B4=BF=E0=B4=95=E0=B5=8D=E0=B4=95=E0=B5=81=E0=B4=A8=
=E0=B5=8D=E0=B4=A8=E0=B4=B5=E0=B4=B0=E0=B4=BE=E0=B4=AF=E0=B4=BE=E0=B4=B2=E0=
=B5=81=E0=B4=82, AI-=E0=B4=AF=E0=B4=BF=E0=B5=BD =E0=B4=A8=E0=B4=BF=E0=B4=A8=
=E0=B5=8D=E0=B4=A8=E0=B5=8D =E0=B4=AA=E0=B5=8D=E0=B4=B0=E0=B4=AF=E0=B5=8B=
=E0=B4=9C=E0=B4=A8=E0=B4=82 =E0=B4=A8=E0=B5=87=E0=B4=9F=E0=B4=A3=E0=B4=82=
=E2=80=9D), and the East African language Amharic (=E2=80=9C=E1=88=B0=E1=8B=
=8E=E1=89=BD =E1=8B=A8=E1=88=9A=E1=8A=93=E1=8C=88=E1=88=A9=E1=89=B5 =E1=89=
=8B=E1=8A=95=E1=89=8B =E1=88=9D=E1=8A=95=E1=88=9D =E1=8B=AD=E1=88=81=E1=8A=
=95 =E1=88=9D=E1=8A=95 =E1=8A=A8 AI =E1=89=B0=E1=8C=A0=E1=89=83=E1=88=9A =
=E1=88=98=E1=88=86=E1=8A=95 =E1=8A=A0=E1=88=88=E1=89=A3=E1=89=B8=E1=8B=8D=
=E1=8D=A2=E2=80=9D) costs 13 tokens, 26 tokens, and 78 tokens, respectively=
, even though the difference in character counts is negligible.</li>
<li>CLEAR tallied the maximum/minimum token count ratio for tokenizers acro=
ss the <a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9Xl=
S2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF623qgz0W8wLKSR6lZ3mqF69GHcvNpSyW1z8zj=
_5x_KcbVXJKGp35RG72Mc3xMVk0K7MN8BtlthSX0pFW64NDL64bY6qxW539Glj88Df8fW3C-FtY=
8YB1X3VDz8_F6mxXB9W6n5Gg32GH3VxW4xVRq36CkKSYW7lWZFZ5ZCghjW6K9_Nn13gr4ZW1c-8=
FR1zpps4W69_8sV10L1l2W8rkNtt3GZnbfW5b_VHR7yVyMrW93SWZM8D4vcqW3cKZw16pthz8W8=
2CJ9K7bg4m8W3g79Pl3nzNpWM5hlcqJXdrTN6nRNxwz54c8W6j4k3s8Bv6QsW8w9lF67hm5LTW1=
n0RzC10DxxNW26Gd7w4VpfNsW6qsjd06xmZXgf4-vTq-04" style=3D"color:#237b94" dat=
a-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"0RwxKT/P" target=3D"_blank">FLORES=
-200 languages</a> (204 low-resource language and script pairs) and, on eit=
her end of the scale, gave the tokenizers an A for a ratio of three times o=
r less and an F for a ratio exceeding 12 times. Many of what were then the =
most advanced, general-purpose AI models=E2=80=99 tokenizers =E2=80=94 GPT-=
5 and Llama 3.3 among them =E2=80=94 got an F, while Google=E2=80=99s Gemin=
i/Gemma family earned the study=E2=80=99s best grade, a B.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
><strong>Behind the news:</strong> This isn=E2=80=99t the first time that a=
 light has been shone on token bias. CLEAR cites two 2023 studies that were=
 among the first to examine the issue.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li>In =E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC=
404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF5s3qgz0W7lCdLW6lZ3pfW5scKW57=
QnY1-W2jds-2809qskW63dfsk52TXHpW3CN4mB2yx84hW8ltkcH814FGHVC49FB7LRQN8W5v4m8=
J4G-9t6W9cfhSq1g9hBpN23FJfR6RxmpW8m-4GM65JXVwW8vHrxW7m91vtN3Ym3vNqcmVBW4Q68=
nv6FDp0DW82cM_h39r2FNW3Bmnhy5VPwDZW2sxXHw8Yhn84VVmdK23j9hHnW8zjFFM3qk1DVW6W=
7TPL3pY70yW12WRGV4MjQbpW6kZJlc338skYW49DNZK15xlmPN3-Rh8lWJyXmVQ5_w12nVrKvf4=
X5X3Y04" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=
=3D"PM1xrqJ4" target=3D"_blank">Language Model Tokenizers Introduce Unfairn=
ess Between Languages</a>,=E2=80=9D presented at NeurIPS in 2023, Petrov et=
 al. argued that tokenization differences didn=E2=80=99t just cost more (15=
 times in their study), but also slowed down AI inference for some global u=
sers.</li>
<li>In =E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC=
404/VX9XlS2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF5s3qgz0W7lCdLW6lZ3pTW1_Ygtk4=
c_n2fW7Q8Nz-2TfBLhW9714Z56D28GyW3JwCky24ZTbTW7PvkkB71qTNYW98ttXr5tV0ZXW1bvq=
Wf8dyjQCN1s-Y3-90YP6N48NJ7pRdF91N646hVwpXDJWN5xHtQWNy56GW1P4xCF6YCl-tW6xg0R=
s36G0n7W1dfwjT1QHnP6W4Gw6fk1TrCFrW3F3Nv063RjPdVbDDVl6HKZ4FW2JmZMC11FwrXW1fR=
QMb5Dw5fhW6Plqm71Jc4y5W8NDY1D3zNN7dVPTG-n7gZNcXW45czcz4TM_9lVPfk356FCrTPf8N=
sD6804" style=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D=
"GfsgLaEu" target=3D"_blank">Do All Languages Cost the Same</a>,=E2=80=9D A=
hia et al. analyzed OpenAI=E2=80=99s popular language model API across 22 t=
ypologically diverse languages and found that speakers of many of them, par=
ticularly languages with scripts underrepresented in training data, were ov=
ercharged for the same content while also getting poorer results.</li>
<li>A <a href=3D"https://info.deeplearning.ai/e3t/Ctc/LX+113/cJhC404/VX9XlS=
2DbV0TW8qTz8v7-Rf_WW8QwHkG5XSKyyN8rPF5s3qgz0W7lCdLW6lZ3mCW2qwNtt7gbvHFW4kyR=
Ry4gvGKCW1vVct48v-GxXW1BJ-w92s6k5WW5z4gy06F384XW4wD6Bk6d6yXvW55K-TH8ZjrcXW1=
K5D6-1nRRz4W12-XHb7qgcp9W9dvvTm34_ZqpW1yTm-Z5_1zyFMm102lh6RC2VVlFkb5qNfc2W4=
jDnk961x6YWW39PH0F1wfxPBN3Q0t-xdqZ0NW1mf8754BJK27W4_rLsW77gVMPW89mmVp3NGhBR=
N6BjRF-s5XD0W4sWW0T5GZ01wW6pxzqY8Vy3DzVQ3Fhx5KrXLPW42rM_v3xsq05f725NZ204" s=
tyle=3D"color:#237b94" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"dSh5rcli=
" target=3D"_blank">2024 study</a> on GPT-4o found that its tokenizer conta=
ined many overly long Chinese tokens, a large share of them drawn from spam=
, gambling, and adult-content web text. GPT-4o handled these tokens worse t=
han GPT-4 did, which the authors tie to how the tokenizer treats long, stat=
istically frequent vocabulary items from noisy training data.</li>
<li>While some tokenizers have improved, newer models within a family can a=
ctually perform worse than their predecessors. In the CLEAR study, Alibaba=
=E2=80=99s Qwen 3.6 had a max/min token count ratio of 13.1 times, while th=
e older Qwen 3 had one of 10.5 times.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Startups and users in emerging markets ar=
e already at a disadvantage when it comes to getting the reliable connectiv=
ity and/or computing power required to use most LLMs. Adding a tax for loca=
l languages restricts the worldwide market for AI and pushes more queries t=
o Roman scripts or other global languages like Mandarin Chinese. This reduc=
es our planetary linguistic diversity to something closer to a monoculture.=
</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
>&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; background-color:#ffffff" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff"=
><strong>We=E2=80=99re thinking:</strong> As linguistic units, tokens&nbsp;=
capture meaning better than whole words or individual characters, but where=
 one token stops and the next begins is still quite arbitrary. We need cont=
inued textual scholarship and ethnographic work to properly capture nuances=
 in meaning within these languages and their scripts. Better tokenization s=
hould be part of that effort too. This will ensure better translation and g=
eneration as well as more equitable pricing.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p></div></div>
